N = 64: the counts of + at b = 3N/8 32 and 32 of 64 (exact);
   with the residues known the two lists differ on 44 of 64 births = 0.68750 (E_N; Inside, Bell's theorem)
   (a) AS DECLARED, the counter family [1, 1] (the birth order the residue order):
       a = 0: the + fraction among B's first N/4 births 0.312; runs in the whole list 4
       a = N/4: the + fraction among B's first N/4 births 1.000; runs in the whole list 4
   (b) UNDER A SEED-SET ORDER (the mixing hash), 200 seeds, the decoders fixed before the run, each right on: first quarter 191 of 400 (0.477); threshold 199 of 400 (0.497); runs (few = the declared order) 200 of 400 (0.500); lag-one sameness 197 of 400 (0.492); halves' drift 196 of 400 (0.490); the runs about 32 (the balanced string's own)
N = 256: the counts of + at b = 3N/8 128 and 128 of 256 (exact);
